Nivel de vechime: Asociat
Tip de angajare: Full-time
Sectoare de activitate: Servicii IT și consultanță IT
Who We Are
 DB Global Technology, Deutsche Bank's technology center in Central and Eastern Europe, opened its Bucharest office in January 2014 and is continuously expanding. The team comprises enthusiastic professionals working in an international environment, dedicated to learning new technologies and fundamentally changing how Deutsche Bank operates.
We're looking for a talented and motivated Backend Engineer with Spring Security hands on experience.
 What You'll Be Doing
Implement highly scalable, secure, and resilient backend solutions using Java 17+ and Spring Boot;
Develop, test, maintain, and document Java-based software components in accordance with requirements, actively contributing to all stages of the software development lifecycle;
Maintain high standards of software quality by adhering to good practices and habits, including thorough code reviews and contributing to technical standards;
Use AI-assisted development tools (e.g. GitHub Copilot, Claude) to improve productivity and quality across coding, testing, code review, and documentation;
Contribute to the team's AI-enabled engineering practices, such as shared prompts, agent instructions, and reusable workflows;
Identify and resolve complex technical issues, ensuring system stability and performance;
Collaborate with BAs, QAs, and stakeholders to jointly develop effective solutions;
Provide support to ensure high-quality releases;
Thrive in a scaled Agile working environment, collaborating with a global and diverse team;
Work on-site at the office 3 days per week, taking part in in-person collaboration, team ceremonies, and knowledge sharing. 
 What You'll Bring Along
Minimum 5-7 years of professional experience in backend software development, with a strong focus on the Java & Spring technology stack;
Deep expertise in Java 17+ and the Spring ecosystem;
Good understanding of microservice architecture, with hands-on experience in containerization and container orchestration tools (Docker, Kubernetes, etc.);
Good understanding of design patterns and SOLID principles;
Proven experience designing and building scalable backend solutions and RESTful APIs;
Experience with relational databases, including advanced SQL and schema design;
Hands-on experience with AI coding assistants (e.g. GitHub Copilot, Claude Code, Cursor) and the judgement to critically review, test, and validate AI-generated code;
Familiarity with agentic development workflows (custom agents, instruction files, MCP integrations) is a plus;
Awareness of responsible AI use, including data protection, security, and compliance considerations;
Relevant hands-on experience with Google Cloud Platform (GCP) or other major cloud providers is a plus;
Comfortable taking on DevOps tasks, such as setting up environments, managing CI/CD pipelines, and provisioning infrastructure with Terraform or similar IaC tools;
Knowledge of and experience with Agile values, principles, and methods;
Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, and a strong team player mindset;
Ability to work effectively in a global, multi-cultural environment with teams located in different time zones;
Willingness and availability to work from the office 3 days per week.
